@@ -25,7 +25,13 @@
 Seismic conversion, into an existing representation that holds every value it encodes: Q3_K and
 IQ3_S into `q6k` (f16 super-scale × int8 scale per sixteen values × code in [-32, 31]), IQ4_NL
 into `iq4g32` (the same table). Such a format adds no execution class, and the plan and the
-assessment's decode demand charge the wider representation's resident bytes. A format no representation holds exactly is not
+assessment's decode demand charge the wider representation's resident bytes. Importance-grid formats IQ1_S/IQ1_M, IQ2_XXS/IQ2_XS/IQ2_S and IQ3_XXS import
+into four-bit resident palette indices with F32 scales per 16 or 32 values. Codes
+are re-indexed and dyadic scale products remain exact; no weights are requantized.
+Q2_K imports with zero-extended four-bit codes, retaining its four-bit scale/minimum
+fields per sixteen values and original F16 factors per 256. Import, assessment and
+native resource bounds charge these wider resident representations and aligned
+planes. A format no representation holds exactly is not
 imported; its model is `Unsupported`.
 Q4_0, Q5_0, Q5_1, MXFP4 and NVFP4 import into representations of their own, moving codes and
 scale fields bit for bit: the 4-bit coded family (a codebook and one scale per 32 or 16 values:
